gcmove 1 fps:30
build {
}
# GRAPHCODE MOVE: THE FOUR-LEGGED BODY'S POSE PRESETS, shipped with the Move plugin. Do not build this file: name it from your own
# file's header with  presets:/GraphCodeMove/Presets/Quadruped/QuadrupedBody  and call its presets ($Stance(...), $Head(...),
# $Tail(...), ...) in your clips. Your file keeps its own skeleton:, ik_rig:, into: lines. No animal ships with it: bring your own
# quadruped, rename the bones (the block below), set its measured rig_ values, and teach the reader with Train.
# MEASURED ON ONE CAT SCULPT, NO SECOND BODY TESTED. Every number of this body is a rig_ value whose default is THE TEST CAT'S
# DEFAULT: MEASURE YOUR OWN. The guide is Plugins/GraphCode/Docs/Guides/QUADRUPED-PRESETS.md (what each preset says, how to
# measure a rig_ value with [readings=(0)], the pad clearance, Train, what is not built).
# The Head and Tail helpers' rig_ values (joint axes, tail segments, the rest face) are written by
# Saved/Research/MOVE-PARAM1/work-quad-headtail/gen3.py from the built rest's readings; rerun it on your body's readings.
#
# THE LANGUAGE IS THE HUMAN LIBRARY'S (/GraphCodeMove/Presets/Human/HumanBody): a preset is a parameterised pose for one body part,
# Name = pose(value=default, ...) { lines }, called $Name(value=...). A value not written is none: its lines are not written. A
# default that is a formula follows the values it reads. raise 0 straight down, 90 level, 180 up; azimuth 0 ahead, 90 out to the
# limb's own side, 180 behind, below 0 across; absolute in the figure's frame. A sided preset takes left=true, right=true; a side
# written false writes none of its lines, so uneven sides are two calls. RANGES: every value an author writes carries x_min and x_max
# beside it: a number outside is refused by name, x=max / x=min mean the end, and a call may widen an end. Helpers (marked
# "not listed") only carry arithmetic for the preset above them; a none passed down a call stays none in the callee.
#
# RIGHT = THE FIGURE'S RIGHT, THE BUILD'S OWN WORD: the character's directions are left +X, forward +Y, up +Z, so the figure's right
# is -X. ON THE TEST CAT THE _L BONES STAND ON THE FIGURE'S RIGHT (its _L / _R suffixes are swapped against the build). Every $right
# branch writes _L bones, every rig_*_r value is an _L bone's number, and every "right / left" pair of numbers below is by figure
# side. shift_right, side, turn and curl_side are positive to the figure's right; Stance's fr / br are the _L legs.
#
# THE BONE BLOCK (the rename list; the bone names are written inline in the presets, as the human file's are). A .gcrig joint is the
# bone from its point to the next point of its chain. Another body renames these throughout the file:
#   part            figure RIGHT (test cat)                         figure LEFT (test cat)
#   trunk           pelvis (the hinge), spine, chest  (not sided)
#   neck, head      neck, head  (not sided)
#   tail            tail_01, tail_02, tail_03, tail_04  (not sided)
#   fore leg        scapula_L (blade), shoulder_L (upper arm),          scapula_R, shoulder_R, elbow_R, wrist_R, paw_F_R
#                   elbow_L (forearm), wrist_L (metacarpus), paw_F_L (toes)
#   hind leg        hip_L (thigh), stifle_L (crus), hock_L (metatarsus),  hip_R, stifle_R, hock_R, paw_B_R, toe_B_R
#                   paw_B_L (toes), toe_B_L
# THE PAW JOINT is paw_F_* / paw_B_*'s point: the end of the metapodial, over the pads the animal stands on. Paw places are
# measured to it.
#
# THE REST these presets count from is the BUILT skeleton's rest (the rig's rest= folds, read with [readings=(0)]), not the
# sculpt's bind points. Test cat (right / left): hind metatarsus 75.7 / 65.1 from the floor; hind paw joint footprint
# (-2.57, -17.72) / (11.68, -15.59), 5.42 / 5.34 cm up; fore blade pivot (-0.762, 11.005, 30.462) / (8.391, 12.185, 30.778),
# shoulder joint (-1.678, 14.394, 25.067) / (8.581, 15.250, 25.900), paw joint (-0.936, 18.420, 4.094) / (6.986, 18.650, 3.742);
# fore bones pivot->shoulder 6.437 / 5.764, upper arm 10.386 / 10.771, forearm 8.716 / 9.037, metacarpus 2.994 / 3.357; the
# metacarpus stands 47.46 / 54.55 from the floor, heading 21.35 / 3.21 off straight ahead toward +X. The trunk's line (hip middle
# to neck) stands 75.74 from vertical. ONE LEG-LENGTH RULE: a leg's length is the sum of its bones from its root to the paw joint:
# hind 22.80 / 22.83 (hip -> stifle -> hock -> paw_B), fore 28.53 / 28.93 (blade pivot -> shoulder -> elbow -> wrist -> paw_F).
# THE FLOOR IS THE PADS: at the built rest the test cat's pads float (each leg planted on z=0 at full weight, the paw joint drops
# hind 2.97 / 3.00 cm, fore 0.77 / 0.76). HindAt stands the paw joint at its pad clearance (rig_paw_z_r/_l 2.444 / 2.342); Stance
# passes the fore clearance (rig_pad_fr/fl 3.324 / 2.982) to ForeAt, and solves its rest stand so all four pads touch.
# SIGNS on the test cat (swings of 20): pelvis fold + tips the front DOWN; spine fold + rounds; chest fold + HOLLOWS (the other way
# from the spine); scapula fold + carries the shoulder joint BACK; wrist fold + turns the metacarpus FORWARD and up (so
# ForePaw.point is the wrist's fold NEGATIVE); paw_F fold + lifts the toes; hip fold + swings the thigh forward. A swing adds
# exactly its degrees to the reading.
#
# KNOWN RIG STOPS AND GAPS (measured on the test cat; the build names each stop it meets, nothing floats silently):
#  1. AIMS ON TWIST-LOCKED JOINTS WAIT ON AN ENGINE FIX: an aim turns the neck, head and tail_01..04 (their twist is LOCKED in the
#     IK rig) only 1-3 degrees, while an aim on the hip works. So Head says turn, nod and jut as swings, and Head's level and
#     look_at, written in the human form, read short until that fix ("N short" in the notes); Tail is swings only.
#  2. HEAD AND TAIL AXES: Head's and Tail's helpers solve on the test cat's joint axes, now named rig_ values (19 Nov) with
#     the cat's numbers as defaults. Another body refits them with Saved/Research/MOVE-PARAM1/work-quad-headtail/gen3.py.
#  3. Hips has no hike: the hike axis is the pelvis's twist, LOCKED (a swing about it asked 10 was clamped to 0). The human Hips
#     has it; this list is shorter. No tilt on Head (a head roll is a twist, locked).
#  4. The chest's fold closes the other way from the spine's (fold + hollows); its stops from the built rest are -81 .. +24.5.
#  5. Back: round=1 curls the trunk into itself (pelvis into sternum 2.48 cm, refused), so round_max is 0.75. Back's round default
#     (it follows lean) is fitted to two points, one of them judgement (a sit at lean 40, round 0.3), not cat data. A lean at an
#     end is written with round beside it. The pelvis's forward fold stop ends lean at 92.24 with round -0.2 (a lean 95 crouch is
#     refused by name; write 92). BACK BESIDE STANCE IN ONE POSE IS AN AUTHOR'S ERROR: Back is swings and adds.
#  6. Tail: tail_01's side stop (+-30) holds the azimuth; past it tail_02 and tail_03 take the rest, to their own 30. raise_min 30
#     (straight down is past tail_01's 125 fold stop). curl=max at raise 150 is refused (the coil meets the pelvis, 2.52 cm). A
#     sit's tail round the side with curl_side alone (raise 65, azimuth 120, curl_side 0.6) is 25 degrees past every side stop;
#     with curl=1 it is exact.
#  7. Hind leg: HindAt away from the rest is not within 1 degree at the hock's 159 FLEXION STOP: a sit's heel 0 at the sit's hip
#     drop reads about 42-47 and its hind paws sit 3.3 cm under the floor; a crouch's heel 35 reads about 40-43. heel=90 on the
#     figure's left meets the hip's side stop (20). Under the rest trunk with the pads on the floor the hind leg runs out of length
#     (reach 0.990, the stifle's 16 stop): Stance lowers the trunk for it. Shin's azimuth stays in the thigh's bend plane (the
#     stifle is a hinge). A straight forward hind paw 0.67 of the leg ahead (a trot contact) meets the hip's side stop (21.1 past 20).
#  8. Fore leg: a planted fore leg at rest is within 0.2 cm of straight, so a paw moved ahead needs the trunk lowered (ForeAt's
#     reach limit; Stance's reach share says so). The figure's right fore under a Stance turn or side stands at its straight reach
#     (1.6-1.7 cm off). A crouch's fore paws stand 4 cm high at the wrist's side stop (15). ForeAt takes the chest's tilt, turn and
#     side beside the pivot (the blade swings against the chest; Stance passes them). UpperArm's raise ends at 100 (the elbow meets
#     the head at 120); Forearm's at 120 (the paw meets the chest at 180). The elbow cannot open past straight.
#  9. Stance: forward_*_min is a formula of drop, lean, round and the shifts (turn and side are not in it). A planted leg out of
#     reach (its reach share past 1) is REFUSED by name. The rest stand lowers the trunk by one number (rig_rest_drop), so the fore
#     legs fold a little more than at rest. The fore pad clearance is the rest heel's: under another heel the pad turns about the
#     paw joint (small, not measured). Stance's fl / fr / bl / br switches carry no range, so the Pose tab hides them: write them.
# 10. Not sayable here: an open mouth or a tongue (the test rig has no jaw bone), eyes, ears, claws; a paw ON a place (another paw,
#     the mouth, a prey point): no PawOn and no landmarks. [as_presets] and the Pose tab's "Convert to presets" read the human
#     library only. An effort on an aimed preset is timed wrongly (time a list of built keys); two poses in one list may not aim
#     the same bone. Posture words (Sit, Crouch, Pounce, Bow) are values, not presets.

# THE FRAMES the presets aim from (each long bone along its length to the next joint; the face is the head's forward). Renamed with
# the bone block.
Face = frame(bone=head, toward=forward, up=up)
LookL = bones(neck, head)
Look = bones(neck, head)
ThighL = frame(bone=hip_L, toward=stifle_L)
ThighR = frame(bone=hip_R, toward=stifle_R)
ShinL = frame(bone=stifle_L, toward=hock_L)
ShinR = frame(bone=stifle_R, toward=hock_R)
MetaL = frame(bone=hock_L, toward=paw_B_L)
MetaR = frame(bone=hock_R, toward=paw_B_R)
ToesL = frame(bone=paw_B_L, toward=toe_B_L)
ToesR = frame(bone=paw_B_R, toward=toe_B_R)
UpperArmFL = frame(bone=shoulder_L, toward=elbow_L)
UpperArmFR = frame(bone=shoulder_R, toward=elbow_R)
ForearmFL = frame(bone=elbow_L, toward=wrist_L)
ForearmFR = frame(bone=elbow_R, toward=wrist_R)
MetaFL = frame(bone=wrist_L, toward=paw_F_L)
MetaFR = frame(bone=wrist_R, toward=paw_F_R)

# #####################################################################################################################
# THE TRUNK (Hips, Back; first layer, not sided): plain swings and shifts, no aim. The trunk chain is root -> pelvis -> spine ->
# chest -> neck; the hips hang on the pelvis, the blades (scapula_*) on the chest. A standing pose gets them from Stance.
# #####################################################################################################################
# =====================================================================================================================
# HIPS (first layer, not sided): the human Hips without hike: the pelvis only, lowered, moved, turned. Written alone the paws
# go with the pelvis (nothing holds them); a standing pose gets these from Stance.
#  drop      of the mean hind leg length (rig_leg 22.81 cm: hip -> stifle -> hock -> paw_B, along the bones, the design's one
#            leg-length rule): the pelvis lowered; below 0 raised. Not written: not asked.
#            Range: drop_min -0.072 (1.64 cm up: the hind legs straight over their rest paws, the design's 22.6 straight reach),
#            drop_max 0.893 (the hip joints down to the paw joints' height, 20.4 cm; the rump is on the floor before that).
#  shift_right, shift_forward   cm: the pelvis moved to the figure's right (-X) / forward. Not written: not asked.
#            Range: the hind legs' straight reach (22.6) over their rest paws: right -8.6 .. 8.6, forward -14.7 .. 5.0.
#  turn      degrees, the pelvis turned to the figure's right about its own up (the pelvis's side axis, vertical at the
#            rest pitch). Not written: not asked. Range: the pelvis's side stop, -12 .. 12.
#  rig_leg   22.81 (22.80 and 22.82, the two hind legs).
#  The shift is read in the pelvis's own rest frame, pitched 2.14 nose-up: drop 5 cm went 4.885 down and 0.187 forward.
#  Worked values (built): $Hips -> writes nothing; drop=0.18 -> the pelvis 4.103 down (asked 4.106); shift_right=3,
#            shift_forward=-3 -> the hip middle 3.000 right, 2.997 back; turn=10 -> the hip line 9.98 right; ends: drop=max
#            -> the hip middle at z 3.88, drop=min -> 1.64 up; shift_right=max / min -> 8.600 / -8.600; shift_forward=min /
#            max -> -14.69 / 5.00; turn=max / min -> 11.99 / -12.00.
#  rig_ values: THE TEST CAT'S DEFAULT: MEASURE YOUR OWN (QUADRUPED-PRESETS.md, 'Fitting your own quadruped').
Hips = pose(drop=none, drop_min=-0.072, drop_max=0.893, shift_right=none, shift_right_min=-8.6, shift_right_max=8.6, shift_forward=none, shift_forward_min=-14.7, shift_forward_max=5.0, turn=none, turn_min=-12, turn_max=12, rig_leg=22.81) {
  if ($drop != none) { shift(pelvis, toward=down, by=$drop * $rig_leg) }
  if ($shift_right != none) { shift(pelvis, toward=right, by=$shift_right) }
  if ($shift_forward != none) { shift(pelvis, toward=forward, by=$shift_forward) }
  if ($turn != none) { swing(pelvis, axis=side, by=$turn) }
}
# =====================================================================================================================
# BACK (first layer, not sided): the human Back on the cat's two spine bones: the hinge at the hips (the pelvis's fold) and the
# spine's shape (spine, chest: fold, side). Plain swings, no aim. EVERYDAY "ARCHED BACK" (the Halloween cat) IS round>0 HERE.
# Called by Stance (the trunk is written once there); a pose without Stance (a jump's air pose) may call Back itself. BACK
# BESIDE STANCE IN ONE POSE IS AN AUTHOR'S ERROR: Back is swings, so a second call ADDS to the spine silently.
#  lean      degrees FROM VERTICAL of the line from the middle of the hip joints to neck, + tipped forward (the human meaning).
#            The cat stands at rig_rest_tilt (75.74 on the built rest); level is 90; a sitting cat 35-45. Not written: no
#            hinge, unless round is written: then the line keeps its rest tilt. The line tips by lean for any round (the hinge
#            is lean less the curve's own tip). Range: the pelvis's fold stops, as formulas of round (96.14 .. -101.76 at
#            round 0; 92.24 forward at round -0.2).
#            A LEAN AT ITS END IS WRITTEN WITH round BESIDE IT ($Back(lean=max, round=0)): the end depends on round, and
#            with round left to follow lean the build refuses it as a circle (lean -> lean_max -> round -> lean).
#  round     -1..1 on the scale, 0 the rest shape: 1 spine +60 (its stop) and chest -45 (the back's top convex, a gallop's
#            gather), -1 spine -25 and chest +24.5 (their hollowing stops). The chest's fold closes the other way: its fold
#            + hollows; its stops from the built rest are -81 .. +24.5. Range -1 .. 0.75 (round 1 is refused by the build's
#            self-collision, pelvis into sternum 2.48 cm).
#            Not written, follows lean below the rest tilt: rig_round_per_degree * (rest - lean), 0 at and forward of it
#            (lean 40 -> 0.30; lean 90 -> 0). SOURCE of that fit, two points: the test cat's gait's Lowered (a built, accepted
#            walking trunk: the pelvis tipped 12 forward, the back left at its rest shape -> 0 forward of the rest), and the
#            page's sit (lean 40 with round 0.3), WHICH IS JUDGEMENT, a paper pose, not a measurement of a cat; no measured
#            cat back-against-lean data exists in the project. round=0 written is the rest shape on purpose.
#  side      degrees, the line bent to the figure's right (-X) by the spine alone, counted from the rest line (the sculpt's own
#            line leans 1.27 to the right at rest): each of spine and chest bends side / rig_side_gain (0.788: the line's side
#            per degree of each joint, read: spine +10 -> 5.88, chest +10 -> 2.00, both to the right). Range: the joints'
#            side stop 12: +-9.46.
#  rig_flex_spine / rig_extend_spine 60 / 25, rig_round_chest / rig_hollow_chest 45 / 24.5   each joint's room from the built
#            rest; rig_l0..2, rig_b0..2   the segments hip-middle -> spine -> chest -> neck: length cm, rest tilt from
#            vertical, read on the built rest; rig_rest_tilt the line's; rig_hinge_forward / rig_hinge_back the pelvis's fold
#            room from rest (20.4 / -177.5, the build's stops); rig_side_sign 1 (the joints' side + is the figure's right).
#  Worked values (built on the test cat): lean=90 -> 89.99; lean=40 -> 40.07 (round followed: 0.300); round=0.5 -> the line
#            keeps its rest (75.80); side=5 -> 5.00; lean=70, round=0.75, side=-4 -> 69.95 / -4.59 (a side under a strong round
#            reads up to 0.6 over); lean=max, round=0 -> 96.13; side=max / min -> 9.43 / -9.48.
#  rig_ values: THE TEST CAT'S DEFAULT: MEASURE YOUR OWN (QUADRUPED-PRESETS.md, 'Fitting your own quadruped').
Back = pose(lean=none, lean_min=$rig_rest_tilt + $rig_hinge_back + (atan2($rig_l0 * sin($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * sin($rig_b1 + (max($round, 0) * $rig_flex_spine + min($round, 0) * $rig_extend_spine)) + $rig_l2 * sin($rig_b2 + (max($round, 0) * $rig_flex_spine + min($round, 0) * $rig_extend_spine) + (max($round, 0) * $rig_round_chest + min($round, 0) * $rig_hollow_chest)), $rig_l0 * cos($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * cos($rig_b1 + (max($round, 0) * $rig_flex_spine + min($round, 0) * $rig_extend_spine)) + $rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2 + (max($round, 0) * $rig_flex_spine + min($round, 0) * $rig_extend_spine) + (max($round, 0) * $rig_round_chest + min($round, 0) * $rig_hollow_chest))) - atan2($rig_l0 * sin($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * sin($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * sin($rig_b2), $rig_l0 * cos($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * cos($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2))), lean_max=$rig_rest_tilt + $rig_hinge_forward + (atan2($rig_l0 * sin($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * sin($rig_b1 + (max($round, 0) * $rig_flex_spine + min($round, 0) * $rig_extend_spine)) + $rig_l2 * sin($rig_b2 + (max($round, 0) * $rig_flex_spine + min($round, 0) * $rig_extend_spine) + (max($round, 0) * $rig_round_chest + min($round, 0) * $rig_hollow_chest)), $rig_l0 * cos($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * cos($rig_b1 + (max($round, 0) * $rig_flex_spine + min($round, 0) * $rig_extend_spine)) + $rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2 + (max($round, 0) * $rig_flex_spine + min($round, 0) * $rig_extend_spine) + (max($round, 0) * $rig_round_chest + min($round, 0) * $rig_hollow_chest))) - atan2($rig_l0 * sin($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * sin($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * sin($rig_b2), $rig_l0 * cos($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * cos($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2))), round=clamp($rig_round_per_degree * max($rig_rest_tilt - $lean, 0), -1, 1), round_min=-1, round_max=0.75, side=none, side_min=-$rig_side_room * $rig_side_gain, side_max=$rig_side_room * $rig_side_gain, rig_flex_spine=60, rig_extend_spine=25, rig_round_chest=45, rig_hollow_chest=24.5, rig_side_room=12, rig_side_gain=0.788, rig_side_sign=1, rig_round_per_degree=0.00839, rig_hinge_back=-177.5, rig_hinge_forward=20.4, rig_l0=11.607, rig_l1=12.224, rig_l2=5.806, rig_b0=72.129, rig_b1=89.475, rig_b2=53.791, rig_rest_tilt=75.742) {
  if ($round != none) {
    swing(spine, axis=fold, by=(max($round, 0) * $rig_flex_spine + min($round, 0) * $rig_extend_spine))
    swing(chest, axis=fold, by=-(max($round, 0) * $rig_round_chest + min($round, 0) * $rig_hollow_chest))
  }
  if ($lean != none) {
    if ($round != none) {
      $BackHinge(lean=$lean, bs=(max($round, 0) * $rig_flex_spine + min($round, 0) * $rig_extend_spine), bc=(max($round, 0) * $rig_round_chest + min($round, 0) * $rig_hollow_chest), rig_rest_tilt=$rig_rest_tilt, rig_l0=$rig_l0, rig_l1=$rig_l1, rig_l2=$rig_l2, rig_b0=$rig_b0, rig_b1=$rig_b1, rig_b2=$rig_b2)
    } else {
      $BackHinge(lean=$lean, bs=0, bc=0, rig_rest_tilt=$rig_rest_tilt, rig_l0=$rig_l0, rig_l1=$rig_l1, rig_l2=$rig_l2, rig_b0=$rig_b0, rig_b1=$rig_b1, rig_b2=$rig_b2)
    }
  } else {
    if ($round != none) {
      $BackHinge(lean=$rig_rest_tilt, bs=(max($round, 0) * $rig_flex_spine + min($round, 0) * $rig_extend_spine), bc=(max($round, 0) * $rig_round_chest + min($round, 0) * $rig_hollow_chest), rig_rest_tilt=$rig_rest_tilt, rig_l0=$rig_l0, rig_l1=$rig_l1, rig_l2=$rig_l2, rig_b0=$rig_b0, rig_b1=$rig_b1, rig_b2=$rig_b2)
    }
  }
  if ($side != none) {
    swing(spine, axis=side, by=$rig_side_sign * $side / $rig_side_gain)
    swing(chest, axis=side, by=$rig_side_sign * $side / $rig_side_gain)
  }
}
# (helper of Back, not listed) the hinge: the pelvis folds lean less the tilt the curve alone gives the line, from the rest tilt.
BackHinge = pose(lean=0.0, bs=0.0, bc=0.0, rig_rest_tilt=0.0, rig_l0=1.0, rig_l1=1.0, rig_l2=1.0, rig_b0=0.0, rig_b1=0.0, rig_b2=0.0) {
  swing(pelvis, axis=fold, by=$lean - $rig_rest_tilt - (atan2($rig_l0 * sin($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * sin($rig_b1 + $bs) + $rig_l2 * sin($rig_b2 + $bs + $bc), $rig_l0 * cos($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * cos($rig_b1 + $bs) + $rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2 + $bs + $bc)) - atan2($rig_l0 * sin($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * sin($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * sin($rig_b2), $rig_l0 * cos($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * cos($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2))))
}

# #####################################################################################################################
# THE HEAD AND THE TAIL (Head, Tail; first layer, not sided). Head counts against the CHEST; Tail is Back's way on tail_01..04.
# #####################################################################################################################
# =====================================================================================================================
# HEAD (first layer, not sided): neck and head on fold and side (their twist is locked), counted against the CHEST.
#  turn      degrees, the face turned to the figure's RIGHT (-X) against the chest. Range -18.6 .. 22.2: the neck's side stop (25),
#            uneven because the sculpt's neck leans to +X.
#  nod       degrees, chin DOWN against the chest. Range -41.5 .. 50.1 (the head's fold stop -49.1; at 50 the neck side runs out).
#            The two share the neck's side room: a turn with a nod can pass the stop, and the build names it (turn 12 with nod 25
#            needs side 30.5).
#  jut       -1..1, the head carried forward and down (1, neck fold 42.5) or up and back (-1, neck fold -26) with the face held.
#  level     0..1, the face righted in the figure's frame. WAITS ON THE AIM FIX (the file's head, gap 1): written in the human form.
#  look_at   a place the face turns to. WAITS ON THE AIM FIX (the file's head, gap 1).
#  How: an exact two-axis solve (neck side outer, head fold inner) on the axes read from the built rest, with jut's neck fold
#  undone first; of its two solutions the one with the smaller turns. Measured on 8 probe poses: the model reads 0.00 off.
#  Worked values (built on the test cat): turn 15 -> 15.00, nod 30 -> 30.00, jut 0.5 -> the face held (0.00 / 0.00), every end
#            within 0.1; turn 12 with nod 25 meets the neck's side stop (asks 30.5 against 25), said by the build.
#  rig_ values: THE TEST CAT'S DEFAULT: MEASURE YOUR OWN (QUADRUPED-PRESETS.md, 'Fitting your own quadruped').
#  ITS HELPERS BELOW HOLD THE TEST CAT'S JOINT AXES AS rig_ VALUES (THE TEST CAT'S DEFAULT: MEASURE YOUR OWN), derived by
#  Saved/Research/MOVE-PARAM1/work-quad-headtail/gen3.py from [readings=(0)] of the built rest.
Head = pose(turn=none, turn_min=-18.6, turn_max=22.2, nod=none, nod_min=-41.5, nod_max=50.1, level=none, level_min=0, level_max=1, jut=none, jut_min=-1, jut_max=1, look_at=none, rig_jut_forward=42.5, rig_jut_back=26.0) {
  if ($turn != none && $nod != none && $jut != none) {
    $HeadQ(t=$turn, n=$nod, j=(max($jut, 0) * $rig_jut_forward + min($jut, 0) * $rig_jut_back))
  } else if ($turn != none && $nod != none && $jut == none) {
    $HeadQ(t=$turn, n=$nod, j=0)
  } else if ($turn != none && $nod == none && $jut != none) {
    $HeadQ(t=$turn, n=0, j=(max($jut, 0) * $rig_jut_forward + min($jut, 0) * $rig_jut_back))
  } else if ($turn != none && $nod == none && $jut == none) {
    $HeadQ(t=$turn, n=0, j=0)
  } else if ($turn == none && $nod != none && $jut != none) {
    $HeadQ(t=0, n=$nod, j=(max($jut, 0) * $rig_jut_forward + min($jut, 0) * $rig_jut_back))
  } else if ($turn == none && $nod != none && $jut == none) {
    $HeadQ(t=0, n=$nod, j=0)
  } else if ($turn == none && $nod == none && $jut != none) {
    $HeadQ(t=0, n=0, j=(max($jut, 0) * $rig_jut_forward + min($jut, 0) * $rig_jut_back))
  }
  if ($level != none) {
    if ($turn != none && $nod != none) {
      aim($LookL, from=$Face, toward=(forward, right=$turn, down=$nod), relative=character, weight=$level)
    } else if ($turn != none) {
      aim($LookL, from=$Face, toward=(forward, right=$turn), relative=character, weight=$level)
    } else if ($nod != none) {
      aim($LookL, from=$Face, toward=(forward, down=$nod), relative=character, weight=$level)
    } else {
      aim($LookL, from=$Face, toward=forward, relative=character, weight=$level)
    }
  }
  if ($look_at != none) {
    aim($Look, from=$Face, at=$look_at)
  }
}
# (helper of Head, not listed) the face asked, against the chest at rest, with jut's neck fold undone.
